+/**
+ * @brief Register a one-shot empty-to-non-empty notification.
+ *
+ * Registers a notification on priority-mode message queue @a msgq: when a
+ * message is added to the empty queue, signal @a signo carrying @a value is
+ * generated for thread @a target and the registration is consumed. Sends to
+ * a non-empty queue do not fire the notification. Only one registration may
+ * be armed per queue at a time.
+ *
+ * A @a signo of 0 arms a notification that generates no signal when it
+ * fires (it is merely consumed by the transition), matching POSIX
+ * `SIGEV_NONE` semantics; @a target is ignored in that case.
+ *
+ * If signal generation fails when the transition occurs (e.g. from an ISR
+ * that cannot take the signal lock), the registration stays armed and fires
+ * on a subsequent empty-to-non-empty transition.
